course: dictionary
lesson: 14907
title: Words that come back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Recurring means happening again and again. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it, because they are its context and often give clues. «My recurring dream is about flying over the sea, and it comes back every night.» The words «comes back every night» tell you that recurring means something that keeps coming back.
explain: Recurring can also describe a problem. «Sam has a recurring problem with his bike chain, which slips off almost every day.» The word «every day» is the clue. A problem that happens again and again is a recurring problem.
explain: In maths, recurring is a special word. «One third is 0.333…» The dots mean the 3 goes on forever. Maths pupils in the UK put a dot over the repeating digit and say «nought point three recurring». That means the digits repeat forever.
fact: Recurring means happening again and again.
fact: In maths, a recurring decimal has a digit or group of digits that repeats forever, like «0.333…».
fact: One third is 0.3 recurring, and two thirds is 0.6 recurring.
fact: Phrases you will meet are recurring decimal, recurring dream and recurring problem.
fact: To check a meaning, swap your idea into the sentence. «My dream comes back every night» still makes sense with recurring, so you know you are right.
exercise: «My recurring dream is about flying over the sea.» What does recurring mean? | *Happening again and again | Lost forever | Happening only once | Very loud
exercise: In maths, what is 0.333… called? | A whole number | Nought point three once | Three hundred and thirty-three | *Nought point three recurring
exercise: «Ella has a recurring cough every winter.» Find and copy the word that tells you the cough comes back. | Ella | Cough | *Recurring | Winter
test: What is two thirds written as a recurring decimal? | 6 recurring | *0.6 recurring | 0.66 once | 0.3 recurring
test: «The team had a recurring problem: they kept losing the ball in the last minute.» What does recurring mean here? | Missing | Happening only once | Very fast | *Happening again and again
exam: Which phrase names a decimal that repeats forever? | *Recurring decimal | Recurring dream | Recurring problem | Recurring cough
